    id: "news-10",
    title: "Made in the USA: Powering Innovation in American Cotton",
    summary: "Cotton Grower highlights American-made ag innovations, featuring companies delivering solutions that support America’s cotton industry. The post Made in the USA: Powering Innovation in American Cotton appeared first on …",
    content: "American agriculture is built on a foundation of innovation, resilience, and a deep commitment to feeding and clothing the world. In its July issue, Cotton Grower Magazine celebrates these values through its special “Made in the USA” campaign, spotlighting companies and products that continue to drive progress across the Cotton Belt.\n\nAll we do is Cotton. All the time.\n\nAs an independent company, Americot ® is dedicated to providing elite performing varieties within the marketplace. Growers can count on the NexGen ® brand for high yield potential, excellent fiber quality, and disease tolerance in the technologies they need to be successful.\n\nGinning Leadership Second to None!\n\nLummus Ag Solutions is the worldwide leader in cotton ginning, whether it is complete facility, a system retrofit, a single machine, OEM repair parts, or the finest in technical service.  Original designs, expertise, innovation, performance, and reliability – that is Lummus!\n\nCotton Harvest Equipment\n\nAt KBH Equipment, our advanced cotton harvest equipment is designed to enhance productivity while reducing labor costs. From high-capacity pickers to innovative module builders, we ensure you have the right tools to maximize your yield.\n\nAs the United States approaches its 250th anniversary, this initiative recognizes organizations that demonstrate a strong commitment to domestic manufacturing, forward-thinking technology, and the success of American agriculture.\n\nFeatured companies in this campaign include:\n\nTogether, these organizations reflect a shared dedication to delivering high-quality, American-made solutions that help cotton producers operate efficiently and serve our nation effectively. Their investments in innovation and domestic production strengthen both the supply chain and the broader agricultural economy.\n\nThrough its July issue and coverage on CottonGrower.com, Cotton Grower connects these companies and their stories with ag decision-makers who value products built and supported in the United States.\n\nBarnes is the senior editor for Cotton Grower magazine. In addition to writing for the magazine, he assists in online content production and in event production. He joined the Cotton Grower staff in May 2008. See all author stories here.",
    date: "2026-06-30",
    source: "Cotton Grower",
    sourceUrl: "https://www.cottongrower.com/cotton-news/made-in-the-usa-powering-innovation-in-american-cotton/",
